    "sourceFacts": [
      "Settings plus ConnectionForm already use two native showModal dialogs; local discard and App discard add a third.",
      "Launcher editor is inline, so its Done confirmation adds only a second native dialog.",
      "Portal changes physical ancestry but leaves showModal stack depth unchanged.",
      "Modal labels resolve to actual h2 IDs and cancel is prevented on the native dialog."
    ],
    "parentReportedNativeEvidence": {
      "buildPrefix": "f544",
      "pid": 27780,
      "observation": "Confirmation screenshot visible but full native AX empty; fresh read and one Tab focus move to Continue remained empty. Fields/key survived Continue, Cancel then Discard cleared draft.",
      "personallyReproducedByThisAgent": false
    },
    "hypothesis": "Native stack depth correlates with the readable Q1 versus unreadable connection/App confirmation. Not a proven WebKit root cause."
  },
  "behavior": [
    "Optional Modal replaceTop defaults false and is enabled only by UnsavedChanges.",
    "With two or more underlying native modals, close only the focused/top dialog before showing discard confirmation; keep React state and lower Settings dialog mounted/open.",
    "Do not invoke business onClose when suspending. On confirmation cleanup, reopen the original top only if still connected and still closed, then restore prior focus.",
    "If original form unmounts during direct discard or App discard, do not reopen the detached dialog. Q1 single-underlying-modal path stays unchanged.",
    "No new modal framework, focus trap, timers, retry loop, backend command or global modal registry."
  ],
